# Shared bnd include for any -test fragment that runs jGiven scenarios in-container.
# A host fragment writes just two lines of its own — its Fragment-Host, and a reactor-relative
# -include to THIS file (bnd's ${.} expands to the dir of the including bnd file; a true cross-jar
# classpath include is a bndtools-workspace feature, absent in plain bnd-maven-plugin):
#
#     Fragment-Host: <the-host-bundle-symbolic-name>
#     -include: ${.}/<relative-path>/jgiven-testkit/src/main/resources/jgiven-fragment.bnd
#
# and inherits everything below.
#
# bnd computes Import-Package from the scenario BYTECODE only. Exactly ONE package the in-container
# run needs is invisible to that static analysis and must be forced: com.tngtech.jgiven.impl.intercept
# — the RUNTIME-GENERATED stage proxy implements StageInterceptorInternal from it, but the scenario
# bytecode never names it, so bnd's com.tngtech.jgiven.* wildcard (which only emits imports for
# REFERENCED packages) drops it. byte-buddy's own packages bnd DOES compute (the Stage base + the
# proxy machinery are statically reachable), so they need no forcing. That single forced import is
# the entire build-time virality measure — bounded, named, contributed by the fragment to the host.
Import-Package: \
    com.tngtech.jgiven.impl.intercept, \
    com.tngtech.jgiven.*, \
    *

-noimportjava: true
